 # The `standard` agent preset: the full coding agent, mounted once per process.
 #
+# ── the acting-roster switches ──────────────────────────────────────────────
+#
+# TWO independent categories, both live, both owned by settings:
+#
+#   kernel — `kernel.enabled` (owned by `kernel-mode`). The persistent Python
+#            namespace.
+#   tools  — `tools.enabled` plus one `tools.tools.<name>` per tool (owned by
+#            `tool-roster`). The conventional roster below.
+#
+# Either can be switched off alone, and both can be on at once. That replaces
+# the earlier either/or arrangement, where the kernel REPLACED the shell,
+# filesystem, search, and job rows and only one side could be mounted.
+#
+# Every roster row below therefore mounts unconditionally, except for the
+# platform gates, which are not roster questions. Visibility is decided per
+# turn by `@deepseek-ai/dsh-tool-roster` (mounted in the base bundle), which
+# filters the assembled prompt — tool schemas AND their guidance sections
+# together — and guards execution. Nothing has to be unmounted to withdraw a
+# tool, so the switch needs no restart: it lands when the model stops
+# generating.
+#
+# The rows the kernel REPLACES are still listed here rather than only in the
+# kernel namespace, because which tools a preset offers is a preset decision.
+#
 # This file is an AGENT-PLANE composition. The roster mounts it ONCE under a
 # standing scope; every session naming it joins by scope parentage, so the
 # tools and prompt sections registered here cover each joined agent while a
@@ -42,6 +66,9 @@
